<title>UK: Granada continues decline after downgrade.</title>
<headline>Granada continues decline after downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Granada Group Plc resumed their decline on Friday, shedding another 12-1/2p to a one-year low at 806-1/2p, in the wake of a downgrade from HSBC James Capel on Thursday, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The stock was downgraded to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Market makers are still loaded up with stock, even after yesterday, and they're trying to get rid of it.&quot;</p>
<p>The stock has tumbled about 18 percent since March when it reached a peak at 984p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
